---
interface Props {
	applicationStatus?: 'opening' | 'open' | 'closed';
	applicationUrl?: string;
	discussionUrl?: string;
}

const {
	applicationStatus = 'opening',
	applicationUrl,
	discussionUrl,
} = Astro.props;

const applicationLabels = {
	opening: 'Applications opening shortly',
	open: 'Apply to review',
	closed: 'Applications closed',
};

const canApply = applicationStatus === 'open' && Boolean(applicationUrl);
---

<div class="study-call">
	<header class="study-call__hero">
		<div class="study-call__status" aria-label="Study status">
			<span class="study-call__status-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
			Independent review pending
		</div>

		<p class="study-call__eyebrow">Study 001 · Open call</p>
		<h1>Help us evaluate nine AI-built interfaces</h1>
		<p class="study-call__lede">
			Human Standards is recruiting two independent experts to complete the blinded review
			stage of our first controlled MCP study.
		</p>

		<div class="study-call__actions">
			{canApply ? (
				<a class="study-call__button is-primary" href={applicationUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener">
					{applicationLabels[applicationStatus]}
				</a>
			) : (
				<span class="study-call__button is-disabled" aria-disabled="true">
					{applicationLabels[applicationStatus]}
				</span>
			)}

			{discussionUrl ? (
				<a class="study-call__button is-secondary" href={discussionUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener">
					Ask a public question
				</a>
			) : (
				<a class="study-call__text-link" href="https://github.com/aklodhi98/humanstandards" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
					Follow the project on GitHub
				</a>
			)}
		</div>
	</header>

	<section class="study-call__summary" aria-labelledby="study-at-a-glance">
		<h2 id="study-at-a-glance">At a glance</h2>
		<dl>
			<div>
				<dt>Reviewers</dt>
				<dd>2 independent experts</dd>
			</div>
			<div>
				<dt>Material</dt>
				<dd>9 opaque interface artifacts</dd>
			</div>
			<div>
				<dt>Time</dt>
				<dd>Approximately 3–4 hours</dd>
			</div>
			<div>
				<dt>Format</dt>
				<dd>Remote and self-paced</dd>
			</div>
		</dl>
	</section>

	<div class="study-call__layout">
		<main class="study-call__main">
			<section aria-labelledby="what-we-are-studying">
				<p class="study-call__section-number">01</p>
				<h2 id="what-we-are-studying">What we are studying</h2>
				<p>
					We gave one AI coding-agent configuration the same specification for a fictional
					community clinic appointment service under three controlled guidance conditions.
					The generated products support booking, viewing, rescheduling, and cancelling an
					appointment against deterministic fictional data.
				</p>
				<p>
					The research question is whether a directed Human Standards MCP retrieval workflow
					changes functional completeness, accessibility, robustness, or human-centred quality.
					Publication is not conditional on a favourable result.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section aria-labelledby="review-work">
				<p class="study-call__section-number">02</p>
				<h2 id="review-work">What the review involves</h2>
				<p>
					Each selected reviewer independently assesses all nine interfaces in a private review
					environment. You will receive the same product specification, scripted tasks, fictional
					test data, and frozen scoring rubric for every artifact.
				</p>
				<ul class="study-call__checklist">
					<li>Complete booking, validation, recovery, rescheduling, and cancellation tasks.</li>
					<li>Inspect keyboard operation and the main booking path at mobile width.</li>
					<li>Score 10 usability and human-centred quality dimensions from observed behaviour.</li>
					<li>Record blocked tasks and concise observations without inspecting source code.</li>
				</ul>
				<p>
					The work can be split across sessions. Selected reviewers will receive setup and access
					instructions privately before agreeing to participate.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section aria-labelledby="independence-matters">
				<p class="study-call__section-number">03</p>
				<h2 id="independence-matters">Why independence matters</h2>
				<p>
					Artifacts are identified only as V001–V009. Reviewers will not receive condition labels,
					run identifiers, prompts, transcripts, source comments, MCP records, automated results,
					or the other reviewer’s scores.
				</p>
				<div class="study-call__note">
					<strong>Please do not apply if you have already seen Study 001 outputs, condition mappings,
					or preliminary results.</strong> Prior exposure would make a blinded independent review
					impossible. General familiarity with Human Standards or MCP is not itself disqualifying.
				</div>
			</section>

			<section aria-labelledby="after-review">
				<p class="study-call__section-number">04</p>
				<h2 id="after-review">What becomes public</h2>
				<p>
					Only after both reviewers have locked all 18 evaluations will we reveal the condition
					mapping and analyse the human-centred quality scores. The final case study will include
					all runs, the protocol, prompts, checksums, outcome data, disagreements, limitations,
					and reproduction instructions.
				</p>
				<p>
					Mixed, null, and negative findings will be publishable. Reviewers may choose whether to
					be acknowledged by name; scores will otherwise use an opaque reviewer identifier.
				</p>
			</section>
		</main>

		<aside class="study-call__aside" aria-label="Reviewer eligibility and application information">
			<section>
				<p class="study-call__aside-label">Who should apply</p>
				<h2>Reviewer profile</h2>
				<p>We are looking for complementary practical expertise in one or more of:</p>
				<ul>
					<li>product or interaction design;</li>
					<li>usability research or human factors;</li>
					<li>digital accessibility; or</li>
					<li>accessible front-end engineering.</li>
				</ul>
				<p>
					You must be comfortable evaluating unfamiliar web interfaces with both keyboard and
					pointer input and writing concise evidence-based observations in English.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section>
				<p class="study-call__aside-label">Selection</p>
				<h2>Two complementary reviewers</h2>
				<p>
					Selection is based on relevant experience, independence, complementary expertise,
					availability, and declared conflicts—not application order or agreement with the project.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section>
				<p class="study-call__aside-label">Honorarium</p>
				<h2>Paid professional review</h2>
				<p>
					This is a paid review. The amount, payment method, and expected schedule will be stated
					before applications open so candidates can make an informed decision.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section id="application-status">
				<p class="study-call__aside-label">Privacy</p>
				<h2>Private application, public process</h2>
				<p>
					Contact details, screening answers, availability, and payment information will not be
					collected in GitHub Discussions or published with the study. The private application
					will explain what is collected, why, who can access it, and when it will be deleted.
				</p>
			</section>
		</aside>
	</div>

	<footer class="study-call__footer">
		<p>
			<strong>Questions about the method belong in public.</strong> Once the study discussion is
			open, use it for questions about eligibility, procedure, blinding, or publication. Do not
			post email addresses, payment details, or other personal information on GitHub.
		</p>
	</footer>
</div>

<style>
	.study-call {
		--study-border: color-mix(in srgb, var(--hs-rule) 82%, transparent);
		max-width: 74rem;
		margin-inline: auto;
	}

	.study-call__hero {
		padding: clamp(1.5rem, 3vw, 2.5rem) 0 clamp(2.75rem, 6vw, 5.5rem);
		border-bottom: 1px solid var(--study-border);
	}

	.study-call__status {
		display: inline-flex;
		align-items: center;
		gap: 0.55rem;
		margin-bottom: clamp(2.5rem, 6vw, 5rem);
		padding: 0.42rem 0.72rem;
		border: 1px solid var(--study-border);
		border-radius: 999px;
		color: var(--hs-text-muted);
		font-size: 0.76rem;
		font-weight: 650;
		letter-spacing: 0.02em;
	}

	.study-call__status-dot {
		width: 0.48rem;
		height: 0.48rem;
		border-radius: 50%;
		background: var(--hs-accent);
		box-shadow: 0 0 0 0.22rem color-mix(in srgb, var(--hs-accent) 16%, transparent);
	}

	.study-call__eyebrow,
	.study-call__section-number,
	.study-call__aside-label {
		margin: 0;
		color: var(--hs-accent-text);
		font-size: 0.72rem;
		font-weight: 760;
		letter-spacing: 0.14em;
		text-transform: uppercase;
	}

	.study-call__hero h1 {
		max-width: 18ch;
		margin: 0.8rem 0 1.5rem;
		color: var(--hs-ink);
		font-family: var(--hs-font-display);
		font-size: clamp(2.8rem, 7vw, 5.8rem);
		font-weight: 500;
		letter-spacing: -0.055em;
		line-height: 0.98;
	}

	.study-call__lede {
		max-width: 45rem;
		margin: 0;
		color: var(--hs-text-muted);
		font-size: clamp(1.05rem, 2vw, 1.35rem);
		line-height: 1.65;
	}

	.study-call__actions {
		display: flex;
		align-items: center;
		gap: 1rem;
		margin-top: 2rem;
		flex-wrap: wrap;
	}

	.study-call__button {
		display: inline-flex;
		min-height: 3rem;
		padding: 0.75rem 1.1rem;
		align-items: center;
		justify-content: center;
		border: 1px solid var(--hs-accent);
		border-radius: 0.4rem;
		font-size: 0.9rem;
		font-weight: 680;
		text-decoration: none;
	}

	.study-call__button.is-primary {
		background: var(--hs-accent);
		color: var(--hs-button-text);
	}

	.study-call__button.is-primary:hover,
	.study-call__button.is-primary:focus-visible {
		background: var(--hs-accent-hover);
	}

	.study-call__button.is-secondary {
		background: transparent;
		color: var(--hs-accent-text);
	}

	.study-call__button.is-disabled {
		border-color: var(--study-border);
		background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--hs-rule) 26%, transparent);
		color: var(--hs-text-muted);
		cursor: not-allowed;
	}

	.study-call__text-link {
		color: var(--hs-accent-text);
		font-size: 0.9rem;
		font-weight: 650;
	}

	.study-call__summary {
		padding: 1.4rem 0;
		border-bottom: 1px solid var(--study-border);
	}

	.study-call__summary > h2 {
		position: absolute;
		width: 1px;
		height: 1px;
		padding: 0;
		margin: -1px;
		overflow: hidden;
		clip: rect(0, 0, 0, 0);
		white-space: nowrap;
		border: 0;
	}

	.study-call__summary dl {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: repeat(4, minmax(0, 1fr));
		gap: 1rem;
		margin: 0;
	}

	.study-call__summary dl > div {
		padding-right: 1rem;
	}

	.study-call__summary dl > div + div {
		padding-left: 1.25rem;
		border-left: 1px solid var(--study-border);
	}

	.study-call__summary dt {
		color: var(--hs-text-muted);
		font-size: 0.7rem;
		font-weight: 700;
		letter-spacing: 0.1em;
		text-transform: uppercase;
	}

	.study-call__summary dd {
		margin: 0.35rem 0 0;
		color: var(--hs-ink);
		font-size: 0.92rem;
		font-weight: 620;
		line-height: 1.45;
	}

	.study-call__layout {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.55fr) minmax(18rem, 0.75fr);
		gap: clamp(3rem, 8vw, 7rem);
		padding: clamp(3.5rem, 8vw, 7rem) 0;
	}

	.study-call__main {
		display: grid;
		gap: clamp(3.5rem, 7vw, 6rem);
	}

	.study-call__main section {
		margin: 0;
	}

	.study-call__main h2,
	.study-call__aside h2 {
		color: var(--hs-ink);
		letter-spacing: -0.035em;
	}

	.study-call__main h2 {
		margin: 0.65rem 0 1.25rem;
		font-family: var(--hs-font-display);
		font-size: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3rem);
		font-weight: 500;
	}

	.study-call__main p,
	.study-call__main li,
	.study-call__aside p,
	.study-call__aside li {
		font-size: 0.98rem;
		line-height: 1.78;
	}

	.study-call__main p {
		max-width: 44rem;
	}

	.study-call__checklist {
		display: grid;
		gap: 0.75rem;
		padding: 0;
		list-style: none;
	}

	.study-call__checklist li {
		position: relative;
		padding-left: 1.8rem;
	}

	.study-call__checklist li::before {
		position: absolute;
		top: 0.68em;
		left: 0;
		width: 0.55rem;
		height: 0.55rem;
		border: 1px solid var(--hs-accent);
		border-radius: 50%;
		content: '';
	}

	.study-call__note {
		margin-top: 1.5rem;
		padding: 1.2rem 1.3rem;
		border-left: 3px solid var(--hs-accent);
		background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--hs-accent) 8%, transparent);
		color: var(--hs-text-muted);
		font-size: 0.94rem;
		line-height: 1.7;
	}

	.study-call__note strong {
		color: var(--hs-ink);
	}

	.study-call__aside {
		align-self: start;
		border-top: 2px solid var(--hs-ink);
	}

	.study-call__aside section {
		padding: 1.5rem 0 1.75rem;
		border-bottom: 1px solid var(--study-border);
	}

	.study-call__aside h2 {
		margin: 0.45rem 0 0.9rem;
		font-size: 1.15rem;
		font-weight: 680;
	}

	.study-call__aside p,
	.study-call__aside ul {
		margin-bottom: 0;
	}

	.study-call__aside ul {
		padding-left: 1.2rem;
	}

	.study-call__footer {
		padding: 1.6rem 0;
		border-top: 1px solid var(--study-border);
	}

	.study-call__footer p {
		max-width: 56rem;
		margin: 0;
		font-size: 0.88rem;
		line-height: 1.7;
	}

	.study-call__footer strong {
		color: var(--hs-ink);
	}

	@media (max-width: 58rem) {
		.study-call__summary dl {
			grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
		}

		.study-call__summary dl > div:nth-child(3) {
			padding-left: 0;
			border-left: 0;
		}

		.study-call__layout {
			grid-template-columns: 1fr;
		}

		.study-call__aside {
			display: grid;
			grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
			column-gap: 2rem;
		}
	}

	@media (max-width: 38rem) {
		.study-call__hero h1 {
			font-size: clamp(2.65rem, 14vw, 4rem);
		}

		.study-call__actions,
		.study-call__button {
			width: 100%;
		}

		.study-call__text-link {
			padding: 0.5rem 0;
		}

		.study-call__summary dl,
		.study-call__aside {
			grid-template-columns: 1fr;
		}

		.study-call__summary dl > div,
		.study-call__summary dl > div + div,
		.study-call__summary dl > div:nth-child(3) {
			padding: 0.85rem 0;
			border-top: 1px solid var(--study-border);
			border-left: 0;
		}
	}
</style>
